Subject: [PATCH 438/443] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on 0437: legacy
 argument rules and a walk note

The typed params now follow the legacy findElJs rules: a numeric ref wins and
carries its snapshot_id, any other ref falls back to the selector, and type
always sends text, defaulting to "". A snapshot taken by the desktop's own
walk (desktop 0.21 and later) carries walk_note, which tells the agent that
walk skips shadow roots, iframes and dialogs in a hidden portal root and has
no size cap. New aeBrowserTypedAction.test.ts unit-tests the param builder and
the blank capture check; the relay suite pins which path each desktop takes,
the real 0.21 payload, a throwing bridge, ref plus selector, a string ref and
a type with no text.
